<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the Mac content filter (roadmap 5.9, step (iii), #988).

  The value is `content-filter-provider-systemextension`, which is the one Apple lists for a Developer ID
  distributed system extension (Codex, #989 `7073424029`, with Apple's entitlement reference). The plain
  `content-filter-provider` value is the app-extension route (a container app on the App Store) and would not
  be granted for this bundle.

  The entitlement is **granted by Apple** and must be present in the Developer ID provisioning profile used to
  sign this bundle; a signature without it loads nothing. That grant and the profile are the dependency Ahmed
  is confirming.

  Deliberately absent: `com.apple.security.app-sandbox` (the extension and the root daemon live outside the App
  Store, and the snapshot handoff needs the path both can reach) and any team identifier (it comes from the
  signing identity, and a placeholder would be a lie codesign rejects).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.developer.networking.networkextension</key>
    <array>
        <string>content-filter-provider-systemextension</string>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
